1
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:12,370
We finally made it to Jogashima.

2
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:14,619
You're pretty excited.

3
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:17,490
It's my first time on a boat, after all.

4
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:20,850
Plus, the vibe here is amazing.

5
00:00:22,390 --> 00:00:24,060
You actually put this on.

6
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:25,340
Huh?

7
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:27,610
Ah... yeah.

8
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:29,729
Ah, it looks like it's about to fall off.

9
00:00:29,730 --> 00:00:30,320
What?

10
00:00:30,540 --> 00:00:31,540
Look.

11
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,530
Hmm... it should be fine like this.

12
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:35,740
Are you sure?

13
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:47,130
He's got great social skills.

14
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:49,839
Is everyone who's
lived in Canada like that?

15
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:52,300
No way.
Akiyoshi is just a special case.

16
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:53,720
I see.

17
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:56,720
I actually wanted it to
be just the two of us.

18
00:00:57,340 --> 00:00:59,929
But Akiyoshi was the
one who invited us first.

19
00:00:59,930 --> 00:01:02,810
I couldn't just leave him out
and go have fun on our own.

20
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:05,940
Sorry about that.

21
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:08,079
I heard they were from Canada,
so we just started chatting.

22
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:09,080
Makes sense.

23
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:09,770
Which part?

24
00:01:09,771 --> 00:01:10,999
They said Montreal.

25
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:11,730
That's really close.
Super close.

26
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,030
That surprised me.

27
00:01:13,031 --> 00:01:14,529
So nostalgic.

28
00:01:14,530 --> 00:01:16,570
I remember Montreal...

29
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:19,900
(Exchange Program Orientation)

30
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:25,040
My mission today
is to ask Chiharu about studying abroad.

31
00:01:27,830 --> 00:01:32,460
But there should still be a chance
for just the two of us to be alone.

32
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:35,629
Until then, I'll just enjoy myself.

33
00:01:35,630 --> 00:01:36,649
We got talked to a lot back then, too.

34
00:01:36,650 --> 00:01:37,859
All the time,
because we're Japanese.

35
00:01:37,860 --> 00:01:38,860
Yeah.

36
00:01:44,090 --> 00:01:45,090
Hmm?

37
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:47,100
What's wrong?

38
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:49,520
Nothing. I just feel like I've
seen him somewhere before.

39
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:58,490
Huh? Toda?

40
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:01,090
Huh? Niimi-san?

41
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:04,300
Hello.

42
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:07,710
Hi.

43
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:44,200
"My Summer Of You"
(Episode 11)

44
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:48,520
Niimi-san,
have you ever talked to Chiharu?

45
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:49,810
Did you forget?

46
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:52,390
Wasn't he the one who picked you up
when you were drunk?

47
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:53,560
Ah...

48
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:55,020
That's right.

49
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:58,689
This is my first time talking
to Akiyoshi-kun, right?

50
00:03:58,690 --> 00:03:59,820
Do you like movies?

51
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:02,650
Yes.
I am a film major in college, after all.

52
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:04,320
I see.

53
00:04:04,360 --> 00:04:07,159
Wait, Niimi-san, didn't you
make movies in college too?

54
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:10,040
That's true,
but I was just in the film club.

55
00:04:10,910 --> 00:04:12,080
I'm in the film club too.

56
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:14,080
What do you think of "Blueprint"?

57
00:04:15,250 --> 00:04:17,920
It's very typical of Director Zaizen.
It's a great piece of work.

58
00:04:19,170 --> 00:04:19,880
Ah.

59
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:23,550
Isn't this area right around where they
filmed the scene of Shindo and Rin meeting?

60
00:04:24,470 --> 00:04:25,630
It was something like this...

61
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:32,370
Hey, mister.

62
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:36,710
That's a nice camera you've got.

63
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:38,570
Are you a professional photographer?

64
00:04:41,280 --> 00:04:43,090
I used to be...

65
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:48,870
Do you take photos too?

66
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:51,180
Yeah.

67
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:52,500
I take pictures of...

68
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:53,960
blueprints.

69
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,260
Blueprints...?

70
00:05:00,630 --> 00:05:02,710
What do you think, Director Akiyoshi?

71
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:05,300
Don't call me director.

72
00:05:06,620 --> 00:05:07,620
I see.

73
00:05:07,760 --> 00:05:09,026
You want it to look natural, right?

74
00:05:09,050 --> 00:05:10,469
It's a college assignment, after all?

75
00:05:10,470 --> 00:05:13,406
No, there's a selection process for
studying abroad, so I'm preparing for it.

76
00:05:13,430 --> 00:05:15,310
Where are you going to study abroad?

77
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:17,040
By the way, what are you going to study?

78
00:05:17,270 --> 00:05:20,360
Wow, kids these days are amazing.

79
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:22,439
Aiming for Cannes or the
Berlin Film Festival, right?

80
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:24,579
It's really not that big of a deal.

81
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:27,099
Which of Director Zaizen's
works is your favorite?

82
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:29,960
I'd have to say his debut film.

83
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,739
I get that.

84
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:34,999
I also like his early
documentary-style works.

85
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,790
Niimi-san is really impressive.

86
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:39,339
I wish I could be as
straightforward as he is.

87
00:05:39,340 --> 00:05:40,340
He really is.

88
00:05:41,020 --> 00:05:42,420
Akiyoshi is completely overwhelmed.

89
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,009
Wataru, are you okay?

90
00:05:46,010 --> 00:05:47,010
Huh?

91
00:05:47,090 --> 00:05:48,810
We ended up hanging out as a group of four.

92
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:50,600
Yeah, it's fine.

93
00:05:51,050 --> 00:05:53,299
Akiyoshi and Niimi-san both look
like they're having a great time.

94
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:54,540
That's good.

95
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:58,790
Though it's a bit of a bummer
that I can't hold your hand.

96
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:00,730
You...

97
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Alright, let's go.

98
00:06:40,630 --> 00:06:42,560
Oh, it's that scene.

99
00:06:43,910 --> 00:06:44,910
That's really nice.

100
00:06:54,650 --> 00:06:55,720
Are you okay?

101
00:06:57,070 --> 00:06:58,710
Thanks.

102
00:07:07,530 --> 00:07:10,880
I know Chiharu's
feelings for me are strong.

103
00:07:39,010 --> 00:07:40,010
But...

104
00:07:46,460 --> 00:07:48,560
The closer I get to him,

105
00:07:55,790 --> 00:07:57,860
the more anxious I feel.

106
00:08:05,030 --> 00:08:06,030
So...

107
00:08:12,030 --> 00:08:15,530
I really do have to go back to Tokyo.

108
00:08:17,770 --> 00:08:19,300
You're already fine now.

109
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:23,790
I will definitely come back.

110
00:08:25,410 --> 00:08:28,960
When I do, I'll definitely
take a picture of you.

111
00:08:43,230 --> 00:08:50,190
So I need to properly convey
what's on my mind to him.

112
00:08:59,930 --> 00:09:03,649
Next up is the restaurant
Chiharu has been looking forward to.

113
00:09:03,650 --> 00:09:04,789
Yeah, that's right.

114
00:09:04,790 --> 00:09:05,790
Alright, let's go.

115
00:09:06,090 --> 00:09:07,090
Yeah.

116
00:09:17,490 --> 00:09:20,410
Was it actually used in the movie?

117
00:09:20,490 --> 00:09:23,560
No. I heard it's
one of the backups.

118
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:28,870
Shindo, who came back from Tokyo,
found out for the first time here, right?

119
00:09:29,330 --> 00:09:33,670
That Rin was actually seriously ill
and passed away while he was in Tokyo.

120
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:37,530
This blueprint left for Shindo...

121
00:09:38,050 --> 00:09:39,370
It's really beautiful.

122
00:09:41,990 --> 00:09:45,060
I can never forget
Shindo's voice in this scene.

123
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:47,580
When he asks, "Why..."

124
00:09:51,810 --> 00:09:52,810
Why...

125
00:09:54,690 --> 00:09:56,690
Why didn't you tell me?

126
00:10:07,330 --> 00:10:09,810
And then today, the
homeroom teacher announced it.

127
00:10:10,430 --> 00:10:13,150
Said that guy transferred schools.

128
00:10:14,170 --> 00:10:16,770
He asked me to keep it a secret
until the second semester started.

129
00:10:16,850 --> 00:10:20,420
I tried to talk him out of it,
asking if he was really sure about this.

130
00:10:20,670 --> 00:10:23,410
But he was absolutely
adamant and wouldn't budge.

131
00:10:30,330 --> 00:10:32,890
So Shindo understood
everything right then, didn't he?

132
00:10:33,310 --> 00:10:35,480
He realized how much Rin
loved the photos he took.

133
00:10:35,710 --> 00:10:38,260
And that she wanted him to
press the shutter one more time.

134
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:40,840
That's "loss and rebirth," isn't it?

135
00:10:41,930 --> 00:10:45,740
That's a theme Director Zaizen
has been portraying for a long time.

136
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:53,000
That's just too selfish.

137
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:56,000
What do you mean?

138
00:10:57,650 --> 00:11:01,110
Because if you just die
without saying anything,

139
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:05,140
won't the people left
behind suffer forever?

140
00:11:14,130 --> 00:11:15,130
Sorry.
I said something weird.

141
00:11:17,370 --> 00:11:21,180
Well, you know, everyone
has their own perspective.

142
00:11:21,590 --> 00:11:22,590
Right, Akiyoshi-kun?

143
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:24,760
Ah, yeah.

144
00:11:24,810 --> 00:11:26,390
Sorry for the wait.

145
00:11:27,250 --> 00:11:29,690
Here is your tuna bowl.

146
00:11:32,210 --> 00:11:33,310
Enjoy your meal.

147
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:07,950
Huh, which way is it to the observatory?

148
00:12:08,220 --> 00:12:11,700
I heard it was straight ahead.
Did we go the wrong way?

149
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:13,480
I can't even make sense of the map.

150
00:12:15,410 --> 00:12:17,819
I'll just keep walking straight
down this road to check.

151
00:12:17,820 --> 00:12:18,820
Okay.

152
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:22,920
Wataru, are you okay?

153
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:24,280
Yeah.

154
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,540
I'll go check over there.

155
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:30,580
Should I come with you?

156
00:12:30,581 --> 00:12:32,040
No, it's fine.

157
00:12:50,470 --> 00:12:52,740
What "favorite scene"?

158
00:12:53,690 --> 00:12:56,040
What "loss and rebirth"?

159
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:02,360
Ah...

160
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:04,720
It fell off?

161
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:16,580
Whatever.

162
00:13:18,250 --> 00:13:20,630
Happy birthday, Wataru.

163
00:13:21,670 --> 00:13:25,340
Whoa, awesome!
It's "The Jet-Black Hawk."

164
00:13:57,880 --> 00:13:59,080
Ah, found it.

165
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:43,590
I asked a local, and we
definitely went the wrong way.

166
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:45,860
Huh, where's Toda?

167
00:14:46,130 --> 00:14:47,906
He said he was going to
check the road over there.

168
00:14:47,930 --> 00:14:50,820
Since he hasn't come back,
does that mean that way is correct?

169
00:14:51,090 --> 00:14:53,000
No, that way is wrong too.

170
00:14:53,060 --> 00:14:54,959
It seems we took a
wrong turn way back there.

171
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:55,960
Huh...

172
00:15:20,010 --> 00:15:21,010
Wataru!

173
00:15:22,210 --> 00:15:24,090
Hey, Toda!

174
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:27,259
We've been looking for so
long and still haven't found him.

175
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:28,970
Could he have gone back to the restaurant?

176
00:15:29,050 --> 00:15:30,880
But he's not answering his phone either...

177
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:34,220
Could he be ignoring it on purpose?

178
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:35,260
Huh?

179
00:15:35,520 --> 00:15:37,360
Because Toda was
acting a bit strange earlier.

180
00:15:37,930 --> 00:15:38,680
No.

181
00:15:38,770 --> 00:15:41,100
Toda isn't the type of person to do that.

182
00:15:43,540 --> 00:15:46,569
Then Akiyoshi-kun, you head
back to the shopping street first.

183
00:15:46,570 --> 00:15:48,440
If we find him, let's contact each other.

184
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:49,900
Got it.

185
00:15:50,070 --> 00:15:51,070
Let's do that.

186
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:56,240
Let's split up and search from here.

187
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,250
I'm sorry...

188
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:01,749
No, Saeki-kun, there's no
need for you to apologize.

189
00:16:01,750 --> 00:16:02,750
No.

190
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:04,130
It's all my fault.

191
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:06,200
Huh?

192
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:08,880
Because I hurt Wataru.

193
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:17,470
Let's just focus on finding Toda for now.

194
00:16:17,900 --> 00:16:19,940
We want to find him
before it gets dark, after all.

195
00:16:20,980 --> 00:16:21,980
Okay.

196
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,560
Be careful out there.

197
00:16:31,990 --> 00:16:32,990
Wataru.
Wataru!

198
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:43,830
Akiyoshi, did you find Wataru?

199
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:47,580
I see.

200
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:48,840
Got it.

201
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:52,220
Yeah, I'll keep looking.

202
00:16:57,220 --> 00:17:01,680
Wataru has been suffering
ever since he watched "Blueprint."

203
00:17:02,670 --> 00:17:05,979
Because if someone dies
without saying anything,

204
00:17:05,980 --> 00:17:10,250
wouldn't the ones left
behind suffer forever?

205
00:17:14,620 --> 00:17:15,620
Wataru.

206
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:16,740
I'm sorry.

207
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:21,900
Wataru!

208
00:17:24,870 --> 00:17:26,250
Listen to me.

209
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:30,210
Stay right here.

210
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:38,560
Because if I take my eyes off you for a
second, you'll run off to who knows where.

211
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:41,140
Even though I had already noticed.

212
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:50,420
Wataru.

213
00:17:51,020 --> 00:17:52,150
Wataru!

214
00:17:58,070 --> 00:17:59,410
It hurts...

215
00:18:04,410 --> 00:18:05,540
Ouch...

216
00:18:16,550 --> 00:18:18,530
What the hell am I doing?

217
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:25,660
Wataru!

218
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:31,230
Chiharu...

219
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:32,610
Wait for me.

220
00:18:32,650 --> 00:18:33,820
I'm coming over right now.

221
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:38,660
Let's just rest for a bit.

222
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:46,410
Does it hurt?

223
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:51,420
I'm sorry.

224
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:55,460
I ended up ruining
our special pilgrimage.

225
00:18:57,860 --> 00:18:59,300
That's not true at all.

226
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:09,600
When you were drunk before,

227
00:19:09,770 --> 00:19:12,750
you kept clinging to me,
and it's been on my mind.

228
00:19:14,160 --> 00:19:15,160
Huh?

229
00:19:17,530 --> 00:19:20,660
What you said earlier about "Blueprint"
was about me, wasn't it?

230
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:32,060
I'm truly sorry for disappearing
without saying a word.

231
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:38,629
If you hadn't chased after me back then,

232
00:19:38,630 --> 00:19:40,179
I would never have been able to...

233
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:41,180
But...

234
00:19:44,180 --> 00:19:45,940
You're going to
disappear again, aren't you?

235
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:48,000
Huh?

236
00:19:49,350 --> 00:19:51,020
You're going to study abroad, right?

237
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,290
I saw the flyer for the info session
in your room.

238
00:19:56,900 --> 00:19:58,070
You could have just told me.

239
00:19:58,570 --> 00:20:00,050
Why didn't you say anything?

240
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:02,870
Isn't this just like before?

241
00:20:06,060 --> 00:20:07,160
I'm sorry.

242
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:09,620
I'm not studying abroad right now.

243
00:20:10,260 --> 00:20:12,900
I was just considering it
if an opportunity comes up in the future.

244
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:15,039
But I wanted to think it through
before telling you.

245
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:16,040
I know.

246
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:18,920
You want to be a translator, after all.

247
00:20:21,620 --> 00:20:26,310
I don't want to stand
in the way of your future.

248
00:20:26,510 --> 00:20:29,770
And I know you don't just blurt things out
without thinking like I do.

249
00:20:32,160 --> 00:20:33,160
But...

250
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:40,190
I just can't help but remember
what happened back then.

251
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:46,620
Wataru...

252
00:20:49,300 --> 00:20:50,380
So,

253
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:54,730
I came here wanting to properly convey
these complicated feelings to you.

254
00:20:59,840 --> 00:21:02,420
But I guess things don't go
as smoothly as they do in the movies.

255
00:21:41,210 --> 00:21:42,400
I'm sorry.

256
00:21:52,020 --> 00:21:54,140
Even though you might hate me for it.

257
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:02,360
I'm sorry...

258
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:04,440
Don't apologize.

259
00:22:05,990 --> 00:22:07,800
I'm the one at fault.

260
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:13,830
Hey, Toda.

261
00:22:13,910 --> 00:22:14,960
Are you okay?

262
00:22:15,420 --> 00:22:16,580
I'm sorry.

263
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:18,130
I messed up.

264
00:22:18,210 --> 00:22:19,000
Here.
Ah, sorry.

265
00:22:19,750 --> 00:22:20,590
Are you alright?
I'm fine.

266
00:22:28,420 --> 00:22:29,986
Make sure you go to the hospital
when we get back.

267
00:22:30,010 --> 00:22:31,260
Thanks.

268
00:22:32,430 --> 00:22:33,520
Sorry to you too, Akiyoshi.

269
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:35,230
We couldn't make it to the last spot.

270
00:22:35,420 --> 00:22:37,100
No, I don't mind at all.

271
00:22:38,480 --> 00:22:40,620
Unexpected things happen on trips.

272
00:22:40,810 --> 00:22:42,900
Oh, Akiyoshi-kun.
Well said.

273
00:22:45,200 --> 00:22:47,050
It's about time we catch the ferry.

274
00:22:49,110 --> 00:22:50,620
Wataru, can you stand up?

275
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:55,250
Niimi-san.

276
00:22:55,870 --> 00:22:57,390
Can I lean on your shoulder for a sec?

277
00:22:57,830 --> 00:22:58,830
Huh?

278
00:23:02,040 --> 00:23:02,920
Oh...

279
00:23:03,050 --> 00:23:04,050
Sorry for the trouble.

280
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:46,056
(Preview for the Final Episode)

281
00:24:46,080 --> 00:24:47,270
I'm still...

282
00:24:48,180 --> 00:24:50,216
(Their summer has come to an end.)
Stuck in that summer.

283
00:24:50,240 --> 00:24:52,110
I'm such an idiot.

284
00:24:53,030 --> 00:24:54,719
Even though I already forgave him once.

285
00:24:54,720 --> 00:24:56,580
This time, it's my turn
to chase after Wataru.

286
00:24:57,300 --> 00:24:59,410
Until you're willing to believe me.
